  <prompt>Consolidate the two near-identical private `getXrmPage()` duplicates (`services/FieldMappingHandler.ts:552-561` and `src/client/pcf/MatterHeader/control/MatterHeaderView.tsx:132-142`) into ONE shared `getXrmPage()` exported from `utils/xrmContext.ts`, and add the missing `Page` member to the `XrmContext` interface (it exposes WebApi/Navigation/Utility/App today but no Page). This is FR-20; task 022's form-buffer hook builds on the shared accessor.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. TypeScript shared-library utils, Xrm host-context access patterns (window/parent walker). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Exactly one `getXrmPage` implementation exists in `src/` (in `utils/xrmContext.ts`); `XrmContext` declares `Page`; both former duplicate call sites consume the shared function with no behavior change; shared-lib tests and the MatterHeader `npm run build:prod` build are green.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-20. R1 shipped a third-copy risk: `FieldMappingHandler` and `MatterHeaderView` each hand-roll a window→parent `Xrm.Page` walker, and `xrmContext.ts` — the canonical Xrm accessor module with `getXrm()` — omits `Page` from its `XrmContext` interface entirely. Task 022 hoists the form-buffer machinery into a shared hook that MUST use this shared accessor, so this lands first. Hoisting `Xrm.Page` access into shared `utils/`/`hooks/`/`services/` does NOT break ADR-012: that rule bars PCF-SPECIFIC APIs in shared components, and `Xrm.Page` is a host FORM API the shared library already uses (`FieldMappingHandler.ts:478-512, 552-561`) alongside direct `Xrm.WebApi` calls in `useRecordFieldValues` / `useRelatedCount`. The established split — components props-driven, Xrm access in hooks/services/utils behind a window/parent walker — is exactly where this puts it (spec "ADR Tensions" point 2). Do not "fix" this by refusing to put `Xrm.Page` in the shared library.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/xrmContext.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/FieldMappingHandler.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/pcf/MatterHeader/control/MatterHeaderView.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/__tests__/xrmContext.test.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">MatterHeaderPcf v1.0.20 parity baseline captured before any code change</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">The shared `getXrmPage()` lives in `utils/xrmContext.ts` beside `getXrm()`. Components stay props-driven; no component file gains direct `Xrm.Page` access in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Code added to `utils/xrmContext.ts` stays React 16/17-safe and framework-free (it is a plain TS module today — keep it that way).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">MatterHeaderView's deep-path import convention is load-bearing: import the shared function via `@spaarke/ui-components/dist/utils/xrmContext` (extend the existing `getXrm` import at line 72). Do NOT "clean up" deep-path imports or introduce barrel imports in the PCF layer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No behavior change at either call site beyond swapping the accessor. `getXrmPage()` NEVER throws — it returns `null` when Xrm/Page is unavailable (both duplicates already do this). FieldMappingHandler's failure logging may stay at its call site if the shared function does not log.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MatterHeaderView is otherwise untouched: do NOT refactor its save machinery (task 022 hoists it into a shared hook; the MatterHeader PCF itself is retired in task 081). This task changes only the `getXrmPage` definition/import lines in that file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">No raw `fetch` to the Dataverse API, no `@spaarke/auth` — this task adds no I/O at all.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Shared Xrm host-context access</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/pcf-build-scaffold.md</file>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Cross-frame Xrm walker" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/xrmContext.ts">`getXrm()` (line 236) is the canonical never-throwing window→parent→top walker with structural `XrmContext` typing. Model `getXrmPage()` on it — implementing as a thin wrapper over `getXrm()` (returning its `Page` member) is acceptable if the null-when-unavailable contract holds; otherwise replicate the window→parent try/catch walk the two duplicates share.</pattern>
      <pattern name="The two duplicates being consolidated" location="src/client/pcf/MatterHeader/control/MatterHeaderView.tsx">Lines 132-142 (returns `xrmObj?.Page ?? null`, silent) and `services/FieldMappingHandler.ts:552-561` (returns `IXrmPageLike | null`, logs a warn on catch). The shared implementation must serve both.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare RIGOR LEVEL FULL per CLAUDE.md §8; update current-task.md.</step>
    <step order="1">In `utils/xrmContext.ts`: add a minimal structural `XrmPageLike` interface (at least `getAttribute(name: string)` returning an attribute-like with `setValue`, `getValue?`, `getIsDirty?`) and add `Page?: XrmPageLike` to `XrmContext` (line 17-22). Export `getXrmPage(): XrmPageLike | null` — never throws, returns null when unavailable, JSDoc noting Xrm.Page is deprecated-but-functional and this is THE single shared accessor (FR-20).</step>
    <step order="2">Migrate `FieldMappingHandler.ts`: delete the private `getXrmPage` (lines 547-561), import the shared function from `../utils/xrmContext`, and adapt `this.getXrmPage()` call sites (line 479 and any others) — cast to its local `IXrmPageLike` if the shared structural type is narrower. Preserve its observable behavior (null on failure; warn logging may move to the call site).</step>
    <step order="3">Migrate `MatterHeaderView.tsx`: delete the local `getXrmPage` (lines 131-142) and add `getXrmPage` to the existing deep-path import from `@spaarke/ui-components/dist/utils/xrmContext` (line 72). No other change to this file.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend `utils/__tests__/xrmContext.test.ts`: `getXrmPage` returns the Page object when `window.Xrm.Page` exists; walks to `window.parent.Xrm.Page` when window has none; returns null (no throw) when Xrm is absent entirely.</step>
    <step order="5">Rebuild the shared lib (`npm run build` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components`) so `dist/` carries the new export, then build MatterHeader with `npm run build:prod` in `src/client/pcf/MatterHeader` (NOT `npm run build` — CLAUDE.md §12) to prove the PCF consumes it through the dist deep path.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify the FR-20 acceptance grep: `getXrmPage` has exactly one implementation in `src/` (function definition only in `utils/xrmContext.ts`; the other two hits are imports/call sites).</step>
    <step order="7">Run the shared-lib test suite; green.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If serving both consumers from one implementation would force an observable behavior change at either call site (e.g., FieldMappingHandler's `IXrmPageLike` contract cannot be satisfied by a shared structural type without changing what it does on failure), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than changing consumer behavior to fit the consolidation.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
