  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep for `function getXrmPage` (and method-form `getXrmPage(`) across `src/` finds exactly ONE implementation, in `utils/xrmContext.ts`; `FieldMappingHandler.ts` and `MatterHeaderView.tsx` contain only imports/call sites of it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`XrmContext` in `utils/xrmContext.ts` declares a `Page` member (optional, structurally typed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `window.Xrm.Page` exists, `getXrmPage()` returns it; given only `window.parent.Xrm.Page` exists, it returns that; given no Xrm on any frame, it returns `null` without throwing (unit-tested).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `getXrmPage()` never throws — including when accessing `window.parent` raises a cross-origin SecurityError (try/catch verified by test or by construction identical to `getXrm()`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`MatterHeaderView.tsx` diff touches ONLY the getXrmPage definition removal and the deep-path import line — no change to save/search machinery, LOOKUP_META, or rendering.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Shared-lib test suite passes; `npm run build:prod` in `src/client/pcf/MatterHeader` exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec refs: FR-20; spec "ADR Tensions" point 2 (hoisting Xrm.Page into the shared lib is the established convention, not an ADR-012 violation — encode this so an implementer does not "fix" it). Note: `.claude/patterns/pcf/pcf-build-scaffold.md` §10 contains a `getXrmPage` snippet in markdown — the one-implementation grep is scoped to `src/`. Task 022 consumes the shared accessor immediately.

Completion note (2026-08-25): Landed `getXrmPage()` in `utils/xrmContext.ts` alongside `getXrm()`, with new `XrmPageLike`/`XrmPageAttributeLike` structural interfaces and an optional `Page?: XrmPageLike` member on `XrmContext`. Deliberately walks window -> parent ONLY (not the third `top` frame `getXrm()` checks) — the knowledge-pattern note's literal fallback instruction named "window→parent," and the "no behavior change beyond swapping the accessor" constraint made a 3-frame widening out of scope for this task (a first draft added `top`; reverted after re-reading the constraint literally). `FieldMappingHandler.ts` imports the shared function and casts via `as unknown as IXrmPageLike | null` (kept its own narrower local `IXrmPageLike`/`IXrmPageAttributeLike` with non-optional `getIsDirty()`, per the task's explicit cast guidance) — its private duplicate + warn-on-catch logging removed; the call-site `if (!xrmPage)` warn preserves the observable "not available" log. `MatterHeaderView.tsx` diff is exactly 2 lines: the deep-path import gains `getXrmPage`, and the 12-line local duplicate is deleted — verified via `git diff` that task 040's `RECORDSUMMARY_FIELD`/`summaryValue` wiring is untouched. Updated `MatterHeaderView.test.tsx`'s per-subpath xrmContext mock to also export `getXrmPage: jest.fn(() => null)` (task 040 hit the identical silent-mock-gap class of bug). FR-20 grep confirms exactly one `function getXrmPage` in `src/`. Shared-lib `xrmContext.test.ts`: 34/34 green (28 existing + 6 new). MatterHeader `__tests__/MatterHeaderView.test.tsx`: 7/7 green. `npm run build:prod` in MatterHeader: exit 0, bundle 59.8 KiB. Full shared-lib suite has 12 pre-existing failing suites (`toolbarLaunchDefaults.test.ts`, `EntityCreationService.cascade.test.ts`, `recordHeader.integration.test.tsx`, etc.) caused by concurrently-running sibling tasks 015/022 editing `hooks/` and `RecordHeader/fields/` in this shared worktree — confirmed unrelated by inspecting failure diffs (stale Notepad-modal-sizing/webresource-name expectations, unrelated cascade-lookup assertion), zero overlap with files this task touched. Self-performed code-review + adr-check (Skill-loaded procedure, applied directly): 0 Critical, 0 ADR violations (ADR-006/012/022 compliant — deep-path import preserved per NFR-08, module stays framework-free, no PCF-specific API leaked into shared lib), 0 lint errors (`eslint` on the 3 shared-lib files clean; PCF build's ESLint step clean). No `.claude/**` writes attempted (sub-agent boundary respected). Did not edit `current-task.md` or `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` per explicit task-dispatch constraint — orchestrator should mark 021 ✅ there.</notes>

